message: "If you use this formal research artifact, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "Lean Klein-Gordon Derivation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Partin"
    given-names: "G. D."
version: "0.7.0-research"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gpartin/LeanKleinGordonDerivation"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of a seven-stage, scoped Klein-Gordon continuum
  readout from the LFM c40 two-field C19 action and centered update. The
  release derives the selected linearized lattice mode, its exact discrete
  dispersion, the isotropic C19 coefficient, controlled spatial and temporal
  errors, and a normalized spectral readout whose finite continuum mode sums
  solve the free Klein-Gordon equation. It does not prove arbitrary nonlinear
  solution convergence, a native massless carrier, or a physical particle.
